<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Persona ability: the traits the bot's owner gave it and the description of itself it writes and keeps.
  The body (bots/floppy/floppy.scx) invokes it as its child "persona".

    recalling { asking <-> waiting } -bot.ability.persona.recalled-> knowing
    knowing -bot.ability.persona.revise-> revising
      -bot.ability.persona.revised-> knowing
      -bot.ability.failed (from memory)-> knowing
    knowing -error.execution-> failed (final)

  Inputs: traits, the invoker's <param name="traits"> (one to 24 traits, each a word or short phrase
  of at most 200 characters once the white space around it is stripped,
  in the owner's order). Traits come from composition and nowhere else: the
  bot never writes them, memory never stores them as their own row, and no
  revision changes them. memory, the <param> (the address of the bot's memory;
  null: no memory). bring_up_timeout_ms, recall_attempt_timeout_ms and
  recall_retry_delay_ms, <param>s with the defaults below.
  bot.ability.persona.revise {text, reason}, which the bot selects.

  recalling: with a memory it asks the
  bot's memory (abilities/memory/memory.scx, decision D265) to select the descriptions
  the bot wrote (query_tags self_persona, subject_ref self, the 50 most
  recent, oldest first) and sends bot.ability.persona.recalled
  {description} to #_internal with the most recent one that decodes as a
  description ({text, reason, traits, kind}; a row
  that does not is skipped, so one damaged row never costs the bot the
  description written before it), else with none. A memory that does not
  answer yet is not an empty one: an
  attempt that fails (logged as persona.recall.failed, "Persona could not
  recall a description from memory: ...") or does not answer within
  recall_attempt_timeout_ms (1 s) is asked again after
  recall_retry_delay_ms (100 ms). When the bring-up budget
  (bring_up_timeout_ms, 30 s by default; the body passes half its
  activation_timeout_ms) runs out
  first, it sends bot.ability.failed {message: "Persona could not recall
  a description: memory did not answer within the bring-up budget."} to
  the parent and wakes with none. Without a memory it logs <log label="memory" expr="'absent'">
  and wakes with none: a bot with no memory wakes with no description
  every time.

  Outputs: bot.ability.persona.output {traits, description} to the parent
  (told to its owner): once on waking (on
  entering knowing from recalling), with the description it remembered or
  none (null), and once after every revision it wrote down. The send
  carries the event's own event:schema, so traits that are not 1 to 24
  traits of at most 200 characters are refused where the event is created
  (error.execution in this session): the persona then ends in failed,
  whose donedata is {message}, so no persona is composed from such
  traits, and its invoker gets done.invoke.persona.

  Offers: bot.ability.persona.revise {text, reason} (text at most 2000 characters, reason at most 500, neither
  blank) is offered while knowing: its parent reads it from the live
  session with <decision:offers>, the event its offerable <data> declares
  with its effort (revise_effort, 2 by default, decision D206), while a
  transition without a cond takes it. The first entry into knowing sends
  bot.ability.ready to the parent once (decision D242), after the output. A bot that never revises is working correctly:
  keeping the description it has is a decision this ability makes
  available and never makes.

  revising writes the description down before it becomes the bot's: the
  description {text, reason, traits, kind: "fact"}, the owner's traits it was written under
  included. With a memory it inserts it as a self-fact (scope long_term,
  kind fact, sensitivity standard, retention retain, content_format
  application/json, query_tags self_persona, subject_ref self; the recall
  orders ties in created_at by memory_id, so two revisions in one second
  keep their order) and sends bot.ability.persona.revised {description} to
  #_internal; a write that fails answers the parent with
  bot.ability.failed {message: "Persona could not remember its revision:
  ..."} and goes back to knowing, and the
  bot keeps the description it had (fail-closed); the bot may select a
  revision again. No private bot.ability.persona.revise.failed or
  bot.ability.persona.recall.failed is sent: the memory's own
  bot.ability.failed is taken where it arrives (and a private event named
  under bot.ability.persona.revise would be matched, and its data judged,
  by the revise transitions' schema). Without a memory
  it logs <log label="memory" expr="'absent'"> and sends revised.
  Revision is append-only: the current description is the most recent row.

  Deferral: a revise that arrives while recalling or
  revising is held by <event:defer/> (scxml.rs namespaces/event) and comes
  back, in order, once the configuration changes, so knowing takes it by
  the same transition as on arrival.

  Logs: persona.description (the description woken with, "recalled" and
  its text or null, and each revision, "revised" and its text),
  persona.recall.failed (each recall attempt that failed),
  persona.revise.failed, memory (absent), and persona.failed.

  Contracts: every event it takes names its abilities/schemas/ file by
  event:schema, and the output names its own. A send or raise whose data
  does not satisfy it is error.execution in its sender, and input from
  outside the session that does not is refused, so no cond rechecks a
  payload.

  Bindings: none of its own (the bot's memory, which the body invokes,
  binds the sql service).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="persona" initial="recalling">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- How heavy an action bot.ability.persona.revise is (decision D206),
         which the cognition holds against each tier's effort ceiling.
         Rewriting who the bot is is deliberate: only reasoning, whose
         ceiling is the whole frame, is offered it, and the earlier tiers
         can only hand it on. An invoker's <param> sets it. -->
    <data id="revise_effort" expr="2"/>
    <!-- The owner's traits, the invoker's <param> (null: none given, which
         the output's schema refuses). -->
    <data id="traits" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The bot's most recent self-written description, or null. -->
    <data id="description" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The selected revision {text, reason}, while revising. -->
    <data id="revision" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Whether entering knowing tells the owner (on waking and after a
         revision, never after a revision that failed). -->
    <data id="telling" expr="false"/>
    <!-- What it offers its parent (decision D242), which reads it from its
         live session with <decision:offers>: the revision, of
         revise_effort; and whether it has told its parent it is ready
         (once). -->
    <data id="offerable" expr="({'bot.ability.persona.revise': {effort: revise_effort}})"/>
    <data id="ready" expr="false"/>
    <!-- Memory: the address of the bot's memory (null: no memory) and its self-fact
         statements. The SQL runs on both engines (SQLite and Postgres). A
         memory id is the next row count as 32 zero-padded digits (neither
         engine's randomness is unique across invocations in Wasm); JSON
         rows are told by their content_format, the 50 most recent by
         created_at, then memory_id (the insertion order), read oldest
         first. -->
    <data id="memory" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The id of each request this document last sent the memory, by
         the state that sent it (decision D265). -->
    <data id="memory_requests" expr="({})"/>
    <data id="description_select" expr="'SELECT content FROM (SELECT content, created_at, memory_id FROM bot_memory WHERE query_tags = ?1 AND subject_ref = ?2 AND content_format = \'application/json\' ORDER BY created_at DESC, memory_id DESC LIMIT 50) AS recent ORDER BY created_at, memory_id'"/>
    <data id="description_insert" expr="'INSERT INTO bot_memory (memory_id, scope, context_ref, subject_ref, kind, sensitivity, retention, content, content_format, query_tags) VALUES ((SELECT substr(\'00000000000000000000000000000000\', 1, 32 - length(n)) || n FROM (SELECT CAST(COUNT(*) + 1 AS TEXT) AS n FROM bot_memory) AS c), ?1, NULL, ?2, ?3, ?4, ?5, ?6, ?7, ?8)'"/>
    <data id="description_parameters" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- Recall's time bounds: one attempt, the pause before the next, and
         the bring-up budget (30 s; the body passes half its
         activation_timeout_ms, so the budget runs out first),
         which an invoker may set as <param>s. -->
    <data id="recall_attempt_timeout_ms" expr="1000"/>
    <data id="recall_retry_delay_ms" expr="100"/>
    <data id="bring_up_timeout_ms" expr="30000"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="persona.js"/>

  <!-- Wake up remembering the description, when there is a memory to have
       kept it in; else with none. -->
  <state id="recalling" initial="recalling_from">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="traits" expr="ownerTraits()"/>
    </onentry>
    <state id="recalling_from">
      <transition cond="hasNoMemory()" target="recalling_nothing"/>
      <transition target="recalling_memory"/>
    </state>
    <state id="recalling_nothing">
      <onentry>
        <log label="memory" expr="'absent'"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.persona.recalled" target="#_internal">
          <param name="description" expr="null"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
    </state>
    <!-- A memory that does not answer yet is not an empty one: an attempt that fails or takes
         longer than recall_attempt_timeout_ms is asked again after
         recall_retry_delay_ms, until the bring-up budget runs out. -->
    <state id="recalling_memory" initial="asking">
      <onentry>
        <send id="recalling-memory-after" event="recalling_memory.after" delayexpr="delay(bring_up_timeout_ms)"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendid="recalling-memory-after"/>
      </onexit>
      <state id="asking">
        <onentry>
          <send id="asking-after" event="asking.after" delayexpr="delay(recall_attempt_timeout_ms)"/>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="asking-after"/>
        </onexit>
        <onentry>
          <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.recall">
            <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.recall"/>
            <param name="statements" expr="descriptionSelectStatements()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('recall')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json">
          <send event="bot.ability.persona.recalled" target="#_internal">
            <param name="description" expr="latestDescription(_event)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('recall')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="waiting">
          <log label="persona.recall.failed" expr="recallFailedMessage(_event)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="asking.after" target="waiting">
          <log label="persona.recall.failed" expr="'Persona could not recall a description from memory: memory did not answer in time.'"/>
        </transition>
      </state>
      <state id="waiting">
        <onentry>
          <send id="waiting-after" event="waiting.after" delayexpr="delay(recall_retry_delay_ms)"/>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="waiting-after"/>
        </onexit>
        <transition event="waiting.after" target="asking"/>
      </state>
      <!-- The bring-up budget ran out with memory still not answering:
           say so, and know the traits. -->
      <transition event="recalling_memory.after">
        <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
          <param name="message" expr="'Persona could not recall a description: memory did not answer within the bring-up budget.'"/>
        </send>
        <send event="bot.ability.persona.recalled" target="#_internal">
          <param name="description" expr="null"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <transition event="bot.ability.persona.recalled" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.persona.recalled.json" target="knowing">
      <assign location="description" expr="_event.data.description"/>
      <assign location="telling" expr="true"/>
      <log label="persona.description" expr="recalledLog()"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- A revise waits for the description the bot woke up with. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.persona.revise" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.persona.revise.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <state id="knowing">
    <!-- Tell the owner (on waking and after a revision), then, the first
         time, that it is ready. One block: an output refused (traits out
         of bounds) is never ready. -->
    <onentry>
      <if cond="telling">
        <send event="bot.ability.persona.output" target="#_parent" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.persona.output.json">
          <param name="traits" expr="traits"/>
          <param name="description" expr="description"/>
        </send>
        <assign location="telling" expr="false"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="!ready">
        <send event="bot.ability.ready" target="#_parent"/>
        <assign location="ready" expr="true"/>
      </if>
    </onentry>
    <transition event="bot.ability.persona.revise" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.persona.revise.json" target="revising">
      <assign location="revision" expr="_event.data"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- What it knows could not be told: end, composing no persona from
         traits out of bounds. -->
    <transition event="error.execution" target="failed">
      <log label="persona.failed" expr="failedMessage(_event)"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- Write the selected description down before it becomes the bot's
       (fail-closed: a description that could not be written down is one
       the bot did not take). -->
  <state id="revising" initial="revising_from">
    <state id="revising_from">
      <transition cond="hasNoMemory()" target="revising_nothing"/>
      <transition target="revising_memory"/>
    </state>
    <state id="revising_nothing">
      <onentry>
        <log label="memory" expr="'absent'"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.persona.revised" target="#_internal">
          <param name="description" expr="revisedDescription()"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
    </state>
    <state id="revising_memory">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="description_parameters" expr="descriptionInsertParameters()"/>
        <assign location="description_parameters" expr="descriptionInsertParametersCompleted()"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.remember">
          <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.remember"/>
          <param name="statements" expr="descriptionInsertStatements()"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('remember')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json">
        <send event="bot.ability.persona.revised" target="#_internal">
          <param name="description" expr="revisedDescription()"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <!-- Not taken: the bot keeps the
           description it had and may select a revision again. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('remember')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="knowing">
        <log label="persona.revise.failed" expr="reviseFailedMessage(_event)"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
          <param name="message" expr="reviseFailedMessage(_event)"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <transition event="bot.ability.persona.revised" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.persona.revised.json" target="knowing">
      <assign location="description" expr="_event.data.description"/>
      <assign location="telling" expr="true"/>
      <log label="persona.description" expr="revisedLog()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.persona.revise" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.persona.revise.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <final id="failed">
    <donedata>
      <param name="message" expr="failedMessage(_event)"/>
    </donedata>
  </final>
</scxml>
